    "summary": "Diagnose REST APIs, check response HTTP status codes (200, 301, 404, 500), and inspect TLS certificate details.",
    "content": "# Lesson 58: Testing HTTP/HTTPS Endpoints with curl and wget: Headers, Redirects & SSL Checks\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 58** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Testing HTTP/HTTPS Endpoints with curl and wget: Headers, Redirects & SSL Checks**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nDiagnose REST APIs, check response HTTP status codes (200, 301, 404, 500), and inspect TLS certificate details.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Inspect HTTP response headers only (-I) with verbose trace (-v)\ncurl -I https://www.google.com\n\n# Follow HTTP 301 redirects automatically (-L)\ncurl -L -I http://jamjoompharma.com\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Use curl -I to check the HTTP headers of a website and identify its web server technology (Nginx, Cloudflare, Apache).\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 58, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Intermediate",
    "read_time": 5,
