    "summary": "Configure passwordless public-key SSH authentication (ed25519) and administer remote servers securely.",
    "content": "# Lesson 59: Remote Administration: SSH (Secure Shell) Key Authentication & Windows RDP\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 59** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Remote Administration: SSH (Secure Shell) Key Authentication & Windows RDP**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nConfigure passwordless public-key SSH authentication (ed25519) and administer remote servers securely.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Generate high-security Ed25519 SSH key pair\nssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"admin@bargisy-eschool.com\"\n\n# Connect to remote server using private key\nssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 admin@192.168.1.200 -p 22\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Explain why public-key cryptography is significantly more secure than passwords for remote SSH access.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 59, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Intermediate",
    "read_time": 5,
