    "summary": "Establish encrypted point-to-point network tunnels across public untrusted Internet infrastructure.",
    "content": "# Lesson 60: Virtual Private Networks (VPN): WireGuard, OpenVPN, IPsec & Encrypted Tunnels\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 60** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Virtual Private Networks (VPN): WireGuard, OpenVPN, IPsec & Encrypted Tunnels**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nEstablish encrypted point-to-point network tunnels across public untrusted Internet infrastructure.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# WireGuard VPN Configuration Blueprint:\n# [Interface]\n# PrivateKey = <ClientPrivateKey>\n# Address = 10.0.0.2/24\n# [Peer]\n# PublicKey = <ServerPublicKey>\n# Endpoint = 203.0.113.10:51820\n# AllowedIPs = 0.0.0.0/0\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Differentiate between a Full-Tunnel VPN (all traffic encrypted) and a Split-Tunnel VPN (only corporate traffic encrypted).\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 60, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Intermediate",
    "read_time": 5,
