    "summary": "Disable hidden background auto-launch items, scheduled tasks, and registry Run keys that slow boot times.",
    "content": "# Lesson 62: Taming Windows Startup Bloat: Task Manager, autoruns (Sysinternals) & MSConfig\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 62** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Taming Windows Startup Bloat: Task Manager, autoruns (Sysinternals) & MSConfig**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nDisable hidden background auto-launch items, scheduled tasks, and registry Run keys that slow boot times.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# List startup applications configured in Registry via PowerShell\nGet-ItemProperty \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\"\nGet-ItemProperty \"HKCU:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run\" \n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Inspect Startup apps in Task Manager and disable items with 'High' startup impact that are not essential.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 62, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Beginner",
