    "summary": "Detect and automatically restore corrupt Windows system files from verified local component store backups.",
    "content": "# Lesson 68: Repairing Corrupt System Files: SFC /scannow & DISM Component Store Health\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 68** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Repairing Corrupt System Files: SFC /scannow & DISM Component Store Health**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nDetect and automatically restore corrupt Windows system files from verified local component store backups.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\nREM 1. Check Component Store Health\nDISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /CheckHealth\n\nREM 2. Scan and Restore Component Store from Windows Update\nDISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth\n\nREM 3. Verify and Repair Protected System Files\nsfc /scannow\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Execute sfc /scannow in an administrative command prompt and interpret the integrity verification report.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 68, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Beginner",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 216,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #6b21a8, #9333ea)",
