    "category_name": "Computer & IT Skills",
    "difficulty": "Intermediate",
    "summary": "Decode frequent Blue Screen stop codes to know instantly whether to test RAM, update drivers, or scan storage.",
    "content": "# Lesson 70: Common BSOD Stop Codes: IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL, KERNEL_SECURITY_CHECK_FAILURE\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 70** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Common BSOD Stop Codes: IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL, KERNEL_SECURITY_CHECK_FAILURE**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nDecode frequent Blue Screen stop codes to know instantly whether to test RAM, update drivers, or scan storage.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Common BSOD Root Causes:\n# 0x0000000A (IRQL_NOT_LESS_OR_EQUAL): Faulty driver accessing illegal memory address\n# 0x0000001E (KMODE_EXCEPTION_NOT_HANDLED): Incompatible hardware driver\n# 0x0000007B (INACCESSIBLE_BOOT_DEVICE): AHCI/RAID storage driver issue or corrupt BCD\n# 0x00000124 (WHEA_UNCORRECTABLE_ERROR): Physical hardware failure (CPU vcore/overheating)\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Identify the recommended troubleshooting path when encountering WHEA_UNCORRECTABLE_ERROR.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 70, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Intermediate",
    "read_time": 5,
    "author": "Mohammed Bargisy",
    "status": "published",
    "views": 210,
    "cover_gradient": "linear-gradient(135deg, #6b21a8, #9333ea)",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-14 12:30:00"
