    "content": "# Lesson 74: Resolving Slow Web Browsing: Extension Audits, Hardware Acceleration & DNS Benchmarking\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 74** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Resolving Slow Web Browsing: Extension Audits, Hardware Acceleration & DNS Benchmarking**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nIsolate slow browsing caused by bloated extensions, misconfigured proxies, or high-latency ISP DNS resolvers.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Benchmark public DNS latency:\n# Cloudflare (1.1.1.1) vs Google (8.8.8.8) vs Quad9 (9.9.9.9)\nTest-NetConnection -ComputerName 1.1.1.1 -Port 53\nTest-NetConnection -ComputerName 8.8.8.8 -Port 53\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Test DNS query latency using Test-NetConnection and configure the fastest secure resolver in your network adapter.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
    "tags": "IT Skills, Lesson 74, Hardware, Networking, Troubleshooting, Cybersecurity, Beginner",
