    "summary": "Understand digital certificates (X.509), Certificate Authorities (Let's Encrypt), and certificate validation chains.",
    "content": "# Lesson 88: SSL/TLS Handshake & HTTPS: Public Key Infrastructure (PKI), Certificates & CAs\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 88** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **SSL/TLS Handshake & HTTPS: Public Key Infrastructure (PKI), Certificates & CAs**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nUnderstand digital certificates (X.509), Certificate Authorities (Let's Encrypt), and certificate validation chains.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Inspect SSL/TLS certificate of a remote server via PowerShell\n$req = [System.Net.HttpWebRequest]::Create(\"https://www.google.com\")\n$req.GetResponse().Dispose()\n$cert = $req.ServicePoint.Certificate\n[System.Security.Cryptography.X509Certificates.X509Certificate2]::new($cert) | Select-Object Subject, Issuer, NotAfter\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Inspect the SSL/TLS certificate chain of your favorite website in the browser address bar lock icon.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
