    "summary": "Replace obsolete perimeter security models with strict identity verification, device health checks, and least privilege.",
    "content": "# Lesson 90: Zero-Trust Architecture: 'Never Trust, Always Verify', Microsegmentation & Least Privilege\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 90** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **Zero-Trust Architecture: 'Never Trust, Always Verify', Microsegmentation & Least Privilege**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nReplace obsolete perimeter security models with strict identity verification, device health checks, and least privilege.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Zero-Trust Core Tenants (NIST SP 800-207):\n# 1. All resource communication is secured regardless of network location\n# 2. Access per session is granted on dynamic risk evaluation\n# 3. Principle of Least Privilege (PoLP) enforced continuously\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Explain why an employee connecting from inside the corporate office should have the same verification gates as a remote worker.\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
