    "content": "# Lesson 100: IT Security Capstone: Comprehensive Workstation & Network Security Audit\n\nWelcome to **Lesson 100** of the Computer & IT Skills Mastery Curriculum at Bargisy eSchool! In this lesson, you will master **IT Security Capstone: Comprehensive Workstation & Network Security Audit**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Technical Concepts & Enterprise Fundamentals\nPerform a full 360-degree security and performance audit across hardware, OS, networking, and cyber defenses.\n\nA top-tier IT professional must possess practical, hands-on diagnostics and troubleshooting skills. Whether managing hundreds of corporate workstations or optimizing your personal computer, understanding operating system internals, hardware health, network routing, and security postures is vital.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Practical IT Diagnostic Implementation\nReview and practice these command line utilities, administrative workflows, and diagnostic procedures:\n\n```powershell\n# Bargisy eSchool Comprehensive Enterprise IT Audit Checklist:\n# [x] Physical Hardware: Thermal paste, S.M.A.R.T. disk health verified\n# [x] OS Hardening: BitLocker active, TPM 2.0 verified, UAC at maximum\n# [x] Network Security: Secure DNS (1.1.1.1), unused ports closed, WPA3 active\n# [x] Account Security: MFA enabled, password manager deployed, admin/user separated\n# [x] Threat Defense: Defender real-time active, offline backups validated (3-2-1)\n```\n\n---\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **Enterprise IT Best Practice**: Always verify backups, test theories systematically before applying major system modifications, and document every resolution step clearly!\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hands-on Student Challenge\nSolidify your knowledge by completing this field scenario challenge:\n1. **Objective**: Execute the full 5-point Capstone Audit on your personal or corporate PC and generate a prioritized remediation report!\n2. Open your terminal or diagnostic tools.\n3. Execute the procedure, record your output, and verify that your system is functioning optimally!\n",
